        "thinking": "Now I can see the full picture:\n\nThe server mounts routes as follows:\n1. `app.use(\"/api/auth\", authRoutes(db))` - at `/api/auth`\n2. `app.use(llmRoutes(db))` - at root level (no prefix beyond what the route files define)\n3. `app.use(\"/api\", api)` - the `api` sub-router at `/api`\n\nInside the `api` sub-router:\n- `api.use(\"/companies\", companyRoutes(db, ...))` - at `/api/companies`\n\n\n- `api.use(agentRoutes(db, ...))` - no prefix, so agent routes mount at `/api/*`\n- `api.use(assetRoutes(db, ...))` and the remaining routes follow the same pattern\n\nLooking at the route registry, I can verify that the path prefixes are correctly aligned with how the server actually mounts them. Continuing through the route mounting, I'm noticing some inconsistencies. The `llmRoutes` appears to be mounted at the root level in the server setup, which suggests it might already include its own path prefix. For `authRoutes`, it should be mounted at `/api/auth` rather than just `/api` since the internal routes expect that prefix.\n\nI'm also realizing that `user-directory` and `join-requests` are returning 501 errors, which means they're not being registered in any of the route files we're currently mounting. I need to track down where those should be coming from.",
